{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors","id":11983,"title":"New Agenda: Traitors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T03:24:37-08:00","id":11983,"title":"New Agenda: Traitors","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i>I dedicate this angel's death to Odin Allfather!</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The God Machine isn't the only game in town. The millions of mortals studying the words of Jesus, Ganesha or Buddah are not all deluded fools worshipping a false scriptrue created by the God Machine. Somewhere in the high cosmos an ancient Mage of incredible power and knowledge bargains with the Triple Goddess to change Fate. Deep in the Underworld the Lords of the Dead peruse their thankless unending duties. The Unchained are not the only Demons making terrible pacts for human souls. The God Machine's Angels do battle with pure beings of fire and energy that act in accordance to some unkowable Principle.<br /> <br /> The Traitors, also called Faithful or Zealots, know this. Some have faith, a holy book and a priest who gives sermons every Sunday, others have seen their new God with their own optical processing units. They are firebrand evangelicals, occult theologians, warrior monks, or a deity's deniable wet-work man. Each one believes their is some deity, superior, equal or just preferable to the God Machine. Each one serves it, seeks it, or worships it in their own unique way.<br /> <br /> A lot, perhaps even the majority, of Traitors first found religion as an angel and fell as a result. They were exposed to religion from the mortals they interacted with during the course of their mission or their duties put them in opposition to the servants of a rival god. Their enemies won and to the once-Angel that was a revelatory experience, a realisation that not only could the God Machine be defeated but that it could be defeated by something <i>better</i>. The Angel falls with a smile, with faith that someone is going to catch it.<br /> <br /> When a Demon becomes a Traitor after Falling it is most commonly a need to believe in something. Humans often need faith that their lives have meaning, for demons it can be the opposite. The Unchained can need faith that their lives don't, at least not the meaing that the God Machine ascribes it. An Angel can fall, a Demon can Sabotage infrastructure, but was it all part of the God Machine's plan? Believing in other gods, beings of rival or greater power to the Machine, can give a Demon confidence that no, the God Machine is not infallible. Other Demons swear loyalty to gods for practical reasons. One might find it's way into the halls of a Lord of the Dead and realise that this is his Hell, he gets down on one knee and swears loyalty in exchange for citizenship. Another demon is on the run, it's Cover in tatters, when a being straight of mythology offers protection for a lifetime of service.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Descent:</b> Traitors usually don't like to speak of Descent or Hell. They are trying to get into a god's good books, calling their deity's domain Hell could be considered offensive (sometimes, Satan or Hel probably wouldn't mind). For most Traitors their Heaven is something physical. One might want their god to manifest before them and open the door to heaven where the Demon can dwell safe from the God Machine's angels. Another might be waiting for its titanium bones and carbon-fibre flesh to ignite in transformational fire so that it may join the choirs of the Qashmallim, returning the purity of purpose it once felt as an angel but this time on the &quot;right side&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some Traitors have promises and agreements from their deity or it's representatives, others might have nothing more to go on than &quot;whoever that guy that spoke to me before my fall was working for&quot;. Traitors with a promise will, naturally enough, endeavour to fulfil their side of the agreement and then collect their reward. Those who have less concrete assurances often try to live lives in accordance with their Gods tenants and have, need to have, faith that in the end they will be rewarded. They do so weather that means trying to live by every single rule in the bible, trying to follow the ideals rather than the literal rules, or spend hours pouring over every meaning of the one cryptic phrase they heard before falling.<br /> <br /> If they don't have enough faith, just a belief that some god has the power to grant them the Hell or Heaven they seek a Demon might turn to occultism. Pouring through popular religious books and ancient manuscripts to find the god worthy of their service, and rituals and sacrifices to attract it's attention and favour.<br /> <br /> Traitors of all stripes can be brutal fanatics or gleeful worshippers of cruel sadistic gods. Many would happily sacrifice their friends and allies if their god demanded it, however the Faithful often believe that their God will, or is, judging them and this can give their allies something to put trust in, or take advantage of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Organisation:</b> The Traitors rarely organise. They don't gather in groups to boast about their god's virtues and reminisce about their shared oppression by the God Machine (or mainstream religions). In fact, two Traitors may consider themselves to have less in common with each other than the average demon. Traitors move further away from the God Machine while the other Agendas remain closer to the common origin and shared experiences of all demons.<br /> <br /> It is when two or more Demons worship the same, or very similar, Gods that they are likely to form a clique. They socialise during religious rituals, collaborate to attract the god's attention (if that is necessary and not considered blasphemous). most of all they watch each other and each others lives: Is there some evidence that it is more favoured than me? Should I be doing more of what it is doing?<br /> <br /> Some Traitors recruit viciously. Not just to their agenda, but they go out and spread the good word hoping that this is what would get them noticed. Others can be quiet and reclusive, seeking to avoid attention that would make performing their deity's tasks harder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Religious Theology</b><br /> <br /> Some Traitors live their lives by the literal word of god, others only have a book with the metaphorical word of god or perhaps even less to go by. They all however have faith that following the way will lead them to Hell or heaven.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Take a Beat when the charachter puts the ring at risk or by following his god's orders, trying to attract his god's attention or following some tenant of the scripture.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The character's faith lets him push doubts away and focus utterly on the task at hand. Take +3 on any action where there is a good reason to believe that your character's god genuinely wants him to succeed.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts: </b>Firebrand preacher, fatalist agent of Karma, the computer who files, sorts and indexes the prayers, warrior monk, hermit guru, Qashmallim in training.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Stereotypes<br /> <b>Inquisitors</b><b>:</b> Do you have any idea what '<i>Ph'nglui mglw'nafh Cthulhu R'lyeh wgah'nagl fhtagn' </i>might mean?<br /> <b>Integrators: </b>You have the right idea but the wrong religion.<br /> <b>Saboteurs: </b>I'm with you here, I want the Machine dead too but we can't win this war without help<br /> <b>Tempters:</b> You peruse fleeting pleasures to pass the time until the inevitable, there is a better way.<br /> <b>Vampires:</b> You traded true immortality in the afterlife for... this?<br /> <b>Werewolves:</b> Perhaps you could put in a good word with your Mother for me?<br /> <b>Mages:</b> I too have seen behind the curtain, there is nothing worthwhile there. Why not help me look elsewhere?<br /> <b>Leviathans:</b> The universe existed before the Machine, I have seen proof. Rejoice, for if the Machine has a beginning it must also have an end.<br /> <b>Mortals:</b> It's so easy for you! You already have a soul.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-22-2014, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T07:09:24-08:00","id":12040,"title":"","content":"I still need to read up on Demon, but this sounds like an excellent addition. An Agenda that fills the gap in they experience as Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T07:28:35-08:00","id":12056,"title":"","content":"Bravo. I'm going to present this as cannon to my gaming group when we start. Fantastic addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/200-totalworlddomination","name":"TotalWorldDomination","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T12:11:18-08:00","id":12219,"title":"","content":"That's really cool. It makes me wonder what other unique Agenda ideas might be out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T12:26:39-08:00","id":12233,"title":"","content":"It's a good idea, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T23:37:04-08:00","id":13217,"title":"","content":"I'd love to play a Gnostic adherent as one of these fellas, with the G-M as demiurge. Fantastic work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:01:23-08:00","id":13328,"title":"","content":"I really like this a lot. Tempted to make it cannon when I end up running Demon at some point. Better watch out for a similar Agenda popping up in the Players Guide (Flowers of Hell) as it does seem to be the obvious missing piece in the types of Agenda presented. <br /> <br /> The only issue I see (which I don't see as a massive one myself, but I am thinking on behalf of my potential players) is that if one Demon does have the ear of another very powerful entity (regardless of if that entity really is more powerful of the GM) and gets &quot;snackies&quot; for it that most Demons do not why is that not the &quot;common sense&quot; choice of agenda? If you can prove the thing you worship is real, present, listens to you and helps you, why would everyone not sign up?<br /> <br /> Obviously, Demons are a paranoid lot and some of them resent the very idea of ever being in service to anything ever again. Likewise, I'm sure a lot of them are just fed-up with the idea of a higher power full-stop. Those seem like pretty good reasons for me, but I was wondering if people could give me some more so I can present them to my players when this inevitably comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:43:13-08:00","id":13351,"title":"","content":"Sure, I can think of some extra reasons for you. Here's a big one. It's dangerous.<br /> <br /> A Demon is for the most part a very small player. The equivalent of a spy who knows too much hiding in a cabin in the woods. Sure the KGB might want to eliminate the potential threat but they've got the whole of NATO to worry about and can't divert much resources to combing the woods. A Traitor is like a KGB agent defecting to the Americans.<br /> <br /> The Americans give you snackies, they have a network of agents who can support you, and they promise if you do a few jobs they'll get you out of Russia and give you a nice civilian identity in the USA. On the other hand you're now a much higher priority and even if you do everything right an American agent might screw up and end up selling you out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even with the theoretically perfect God (lets call it The Gnostic Creator above the G-M Demiurge) which is morally pure, more powerful than the G-M* and has no angels who might reveal your name to the G-M. You're still a much bigger target for allying yourself with it. Even if the G-M can't get your name by torturing the Creator's angels, it can still notice that a raid fits the Creator's MO and make catching the perpetrator - you - the top priority.<br /> <br /> <br /> The nice thing about this is that the more snackies a god gives loyal Demons, the more active it is and the more it threatens the G-M. So the bonuses and threats should balance out nicely.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Though evidently, not powerful enough to destroy it easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=13328#post13328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Better watch out for a similar Agenda popping up in the Players Guide (Flowers of Hell) as it does seem to be the obvious missing piece in the types of Agenda presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it does. Then I can do a little validation dance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have noticed that there hasn't been any of the writers on here, unlike the other Demon homebrew, so maybe that's a sign that they don't want to give spoilers yet.<br /> <br /> It does make sense to push it back to Flowers of Hell, that would give them the time and wordcount to address other gods. I'm mostly counting on you guys having read other WoD gamelines or a mythology book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And thanks for the kind words everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-18-2013, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:39:54-08:00","id":13551,"title":"","content":"Simpler point: You have to prove and find the gods you're turning to and trying to get to give a shit about you.<br /> <br /> It's like Fallen's Luciferans, except with other power bases and more haggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:14:52-08:00","id":13572,"title":"","content":"Reason Not To Be A &quot;Traitor&quot; (From the Demon's Perspective) -- It's too good to be true. Seriously. You have the God Machine, an unknowable super being that you know for a fact exists. This being has made it a point to lie, deceive, con, scheme, manipulate, and kill to get what it wants, whatever cosmic level desire it has. It is at least 15 moves ahead at any given time and only through breaking the rules and incredible luck and ingenuity are you able to steer clear of it, much less do anything significant about it.<br /> <br /> A demon Falls, breaks free from the God Machine, and becomes an unknown quantity, a free radical. Then, some days, weeks, months, however long after the fall, which is a nanosecond in Cosmic Superpower time some other &quot;Equally omnipotent&quot; superbeing just happens to show up and offer &quot;benefits&quot; in exchange for doing tasks that further its agenda. An agenda which it swears are counter to the God Machine but definitely gives the demon something to do other than &quot;whatever it wants&quot;. <br /> <br /> After all, who knows what would happen to the &quot;Alternative Power&quot;'s ideals if there was just some rogue demon running around. <br /> And it's not like cosmic beings lie, that's just silly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:41:43-08:00","id":13589,"title":"","content":"Double Post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T00:23:19-08:00","id":13826,"title":"","content":"I would suggest a name change; almost every Demon could justifiably call himself a Traitor. Faithful and Zealot are a bit more evocative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:12:35-08:00","id":14348,"title":"","content":"Note that each official Agenda has multiple names. Inquisitors are also Watchers or Paranoids; Integrators are also Idealists or Turncoats; Saboteurs are also Thugs or Soldiers; Tempters are also Decadents or Builders. Given the similarity between \u201cTurncoat\u201d and \u201cTraitor\u201d, I agree that you probably want to rename this Agenda \u2014 if it\u2019s even appropriate Agenda material.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love the concept that you\u2019re after here; but I think it would be better implemented as a new kind of Agency that\u2019s run by the demon\u2019s new sponsor. Agendas are about what kind of jobs you do; this is more about who you work for. The one caveat is the role that Integrators would play in these \u201cForeign Agencies\u201d. I see two dominant options: either the Integrator is seeking \u201ccitizenship\u201d as it were with its new patron (e.g., a <i>qashmal</i>-in-training), or he\u2019s trying to become a \u201csleeper agent\u201d within the God-Machine on his new master\u2019s behalf. That is, he\u2019s seeking to integrate with either his new boss or his old boss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T02:34:13-08:00","id":14610,"title":"","content":"I like the name Traitor and I think that if demons can talk about how they want to go to hell they can find positive meanings in other negative words. Even the similarity between Turncoat and Traitor isn't a bad thing; Both Traitors and Integrators can betray other demons for much of the same reasons.<br /> <br /> As for the Agencies. It was always my intent that such things exist, but making it an Agenda is absolutely necessary to include the theme of faith. If you limit it to agencies run by sponsors you limit it to gods who provably exist. There has to be room for Demons who have some cryptic clue, faith, and little else. If you need evidence that this is an appropriate Agenda concept I direct you to most of the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:32:11-08:00","id":30554,"title":"","content":"Nifty! Stolen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:26:19-08:00","id":31383,"title":"","content":"And then there are of course the Demons who become traitors and evangelize (to a degree) to their peers and it turns out the whole thing was yet another con run by the God Machine who ends up cashing in after that Traitor cell gets big enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T01:51:51-08:00","id":31551,"title":"","content":"All I see from this is a narrow subsect of Integrators, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T02:19:50-08:00","id":31555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=31383#post31383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there are of course the Demons who become traitors and evangelize (to a degree) to their peers and it turns out the whole thing was yet another con run by the God Machine who ends up cashing in after that Traitor cell gets big enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that happens. Though if you really want to mess with your players, make the Angels your PC Integrator is working with turn out to be Lunes in disguise. It's the last thing they'd ever suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T19:00:01-08:00","id":32071,"title":"","content":"These Defectors are certainly interesting...might have them show up later in my chronicle.<br /> If it ever gets started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T08:41:17-08:00","id":32431,"title":"","content":"Edit: Replied to wrong thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 12-18-2013, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:53:08-07:00","id":204461,"title":"","content":"This... This is beautiful. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=31551#post31551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I see from this is a narrow subsect of Integrators, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? The premise is the idea that the Machine(or the Idol, Demiurge, Morningstar, or whatever the Turncoat wants to call it) is NOT the true master of the universe. In all honesty, I'd call it the Integrator's exact opposite if it weren't for the Thugs.(I'm really relying on what I've heard of the Unchained, so I might be wrong.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:58:21-07:00","id":204484,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Traitor concept is to embrace the other, somewhat akin to the Ordo's desire to become a whole new breed of monster. Sabotuers want to kill the God-Machine, the Integrators want to return to the God-Machine, and the Traitors wants to leave it all behind and join a different host.<br /> <br /> If it is a subset of something, it's a Tempter philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T19:22:30-07:00","id":204532,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that this is a sub-faction of Turncoats in Flowers. Still, it is a very shiny piece of work and I believe it pre-dates Flowers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T10:10:02-07:00","id":205111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=204532#post204532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that this is a sub-faction of Turncoats in Flowers. Still, it is a very shiny piece of work and I believe it pre-dates Flowers</div> </div> </div> </div> It predates Demon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nothing so special about that honestly. I wrote it after reading the kickstarter preview but before the book was released.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can understand the point of view saying that this is a subgroup of Turncoats, from a birds eye view both have the exact same goal: trying to impress a deity and want to be accepted as it's servant.<br /> <br /> But because of how fundamentally important a demon's views on the G-M are to a Demon charachter, I think that the two Agenda's having opposite views on the G-M is more than enough to justify seperating them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:07:58-07:00","id":205143,"title":"","content":"I like it, though I kind of feel that it is a bit superfluous when you look at the Integrators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:16:24-07:00","id":205154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=205111#post205111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It predates Demon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nothing so special about that honestly. I wrote it after reading the kickstarter preview but before the book was released.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can understand the point of view saying that this is a subgroup of Turncoats, from a birds eye view both have the exact same goal: trying to impress a deity and want to be accepted as it's servant.<br /> <br /> But because of how fundamentally important a demon's views on the G-M are to a Demon charachter, I think that the two Agenda's having opposite views on the G-M is more than enough to justify seperating them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know and I'm sorry if I gave you the wrong impression; I like it.<br /> Truthfully it got mt thinking of doing extended write ups for the sub-factions with alternate conditions. Which is how I'd intergrate it into my WoD. That doesn't mean they can't work as a stand alone group; obviously they do. It just means I felt the need to season it to my taste if I were to run a game.<br /> <br /> BTW; big fan of yours Raven. Keep up the good work, your royal highness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T10:47:36-08:00","id":312403,"title":"","content":"After looking through the Kickstarter PDF, I thought to put my head to how the hybrid Agendas might work: <br /> \u2022Saboteur-Traitor: Perhaps the most obvious, these are holy warriors of every stripe, from noble(if bitter) paladins to terrorists with a cause, with a mind to poison the hearts of mortals to &quot;the demons in our midst!&quot;<br /> \u2022Integrator-Traitor: A difficult mix, only rivaled by Integrator-Saboteurs. In the end, the best idea I have for these are missionaries who hope to find a way to &quot;infect&quot; the Machine with their personal ideology through merging with it. <br /> \u2022Inquisitor-Traitor: Theologians and Occultists, they believe their God requires them to learn or discover something, or that their knowledge will earn them salvation. Tend to have greater knowledge of other supernaturals than most Inquisitors. <br /> \u2022Tempter-Traitors: Patrons and Priests , the ones who put a lot in the collection plate either because they can or because they think they need to buy salvation. Tend to be some form of ethical hedonist as opposed to their less constrained counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:13:37-08:00","id":313217,"title":"","content":"I love your idea but If you don't mind I'm planning to modify it a little bit an twist it: The deity that they are worshiping? its the devil, as in the literal devil. He is the first fallen, the first angel that managed to escape the god machine. Through cunning, perseverance and intelligence he managed to survive and grow in power till it became something else. Transcending any other demon he became a god, a master of exploits and embeds on a whole new level, the ultimate trickster god aware of all of realities cheats and shortcuts. However he is not at the level of the god machine, at least not yet. He needs help and for that he recruits demons, through cults, religions and other organizations he calls those desperate to believe in another power capable of facing the god machine. The ultimate master liar, he tells them what they want to hear and brings them in with promises of ultimate freedom. When the time is right and he has accumulated enough power and followers then he will rise his army and dethrone the god machine. The thing is what will happen afterwards? will the demons awake to a world of true freedom in which they will be able to do do whatever they want without fear of being captured by an almighty being? or will they just help a despot to claim power from another despot? that is something for the player characters to find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:01:14-08:00","id":313315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=313217#post313217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its the devil, as in the literal devil. He is the first fallen, the first angel that managed to escape the god machine. Through cunning, perseverance and intelligence he managed to survive and grow in power till it became something else. Transcending any other demon he became a god, a master of exploits and embeds on a whole new level, the ultimate trickster god aware of all of realities cheats and shortcuts. However he is not at the level of the god machine, at least not yet. He needs help and for that he recruits demons, through cults, religions and other organizations he calls those desperate to believe in another power capable of facing the god machine. The ultimate master liar, he tells them what they want to hear and brings them in with promises of ultimate freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could be interested in my Fallen fan Agenda. Here is sum up<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Fallen</b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Better to reign in Hell, then serve in Heavan</i></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Demons are sinners. They sinned against God-Machine as angels, and were cast away in return. They sin to protect they Covers, or sin against them. And they sin like any other human, even if they aren\u2019t ones. Truly, to be a demon, is to be slave to the sin. Fallen are it\u2019s masters.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness, sin is power. People feel better if they do \u201cbad things\u201d in name of they Vice. Monsters of the night rave in they darker side, gaining strength in return. Fallen are demons that after rebelion against God-Machine were confronted with existence as creature of Vice. After the Fall, they could empower by serving it. Also, sinning is so sweet.<br /> <br /> And then they find there is literal Hell. Not metaphorical dimension of freedom most demons looking for. But real, Old Testament type Hell. Many call it Inferno. But to Fallen it\u2019s called home. Or at least they want to. For now, it\u2019s place were they Demon Prince patrons live.<br /> <br /> Those ancient beings, old as humanity itself, are very interested in once angels, now demons.They send they lesser servants, spirits, ghosts and other things transformed by the sins they serve. And those massangers are preaching to Unchained so they coud join in Inferno. Some of them do. And so Fall lead to the Fallen.<br /> <br /> But of course they don't forget about God-Machine. As false tyrant that once rules they lives, it should be stopped. Or at least every beautiful angel he makes been brought to Inferno's Hosts. And Fallen will make them Fall.<br /> <br /> <b>The Descent:</b> Most Unchained wants freedom. They look for Hell in what there aren\u2019t any masters and slaves, only themselves. But without other beings, there isn\u2019t any sociaty, there isn\u2019t hierarchy. <i>Hell is empty and all the devils are here</i> - like they say. But Fallen don\u2019t want to be alone. As once angels, they crave for belonging, orders, purpose. But they can\u2019t return to the God-Machine. They found human side in themselves, individuality, identity.They don\u2019t want to loose those precious gifts of Fall. And so they decide they will reign in literall Hell instead.<br /> <br /> Fallen are both masters and slaves. They work for one of the great Patrons, doing \u201chis work\u201d. But always dreaming on the day when they walk in to Inferno, and took the throne for themselves. They will finally be those that send commands, not obeying them.<br /> <br /> But for now, they join with rest of Unchained. They forging Vice in to powerful tool of they both inner strength and influence on others, They preach to demons about they own free will, and that they should rule. They tempt angels in to Fall. And of course, they hide outside of eyes of God-Machine, as it hunts the like the rest of the kind. But at least they have purpose in they life. Someday, when they will be powerful enough, they will Descent in to Inferno and be it\u2019s masters. Now will they gather the sins of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Fallen join in loose cults dedicated to one of Patrons. They idealise Seven Deadly Sins, working to sustain it in the world, and by it, empowering themselves for they Descent. From time to time they make loose alliances between cults, especially, as they local mission dictates help from in name of many sins.<br /> <br /> Demon Prince Patrons of Fallen in Inferno:<ul><li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucifer\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a>: Pride</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammon\" target=\"_blank\">Mammon</a>: Greed</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmodai\" target=\"_blank\">Asmodeus</a>: Lust</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leviathan\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan</a>: Envy</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beelzebub\" target=\"_blank\">Beelzebub</a>: Gluttony</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satan\" target=\"_blank\">Satan</a>: Wrath</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belphegor\" target=\"_blank\">Belphegor</a>: Sloth</li> </ul>But outside they misions, they are totally free. Most join rest of Unchained in they rings, becoming priest- or advisor-like figures, encouraging individuality and free reign of demons. Of course, they play and scheme they on they're comrades, but helping them in the way none the less.<br /> <br /> Many Fallen are ones Integrators, now converted when they see that by the side of God-Machine they will be only soulless drones at best, destroyed at worst. Confronted with existence of Inferno, they choose they own side. Now have order and missions they lingered, but also work on they own terms. They will join hierarchy, once more, only it is they who would be in charge of it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sterotypes</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Inqusitors:</b> Your knowledge don\u2019t lead you to power, if you don\u2019t take actions.<br /> <b>Integrators:</b> Our misguided brothers and sisters, it\u2019s pity you still don\u2019t see your are just slaves.<br /> <b>Saboteures:</b> Still playing this silly wargame with God-Machine? Your choice, but I\u2019m focused on more grander undertacking right now.<br /> <b>Tempters:</b> Hedonism is good, but you still need commitment to achieve something.<br /> <b>Werewolves:</b> One needless rage is a tool in others great plan.<br /> <b>Mages:</b> You command the \u201cdemons\u201d, yet you can\u2019t master your own sins.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of it is to look in my own cosmological bent on the <b>DtD</b> setting - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/213767-more-classical-demons-and-angels-setting-hack\">here is it in full</a>.<br /> <br /> Now looking on it, I think that my Fallen and Exalted Unchained could easily be just specific subset of yours Traitors Agenda, <b>Raven</b>. But I would be more in favor of renaming them to Zealots in general, because Turncoats is specifically Integrators thing - Integrators are, really, betraying they Unchained kind with vision to return to source they run from, the God Machine. Zealots, most of time, want lead they new brethren to the things they run from only to be taken back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:13:53-08:00","id":313322,"title":"","content":"Cool! thanks a lot wyrdhamster <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T00:31:36-08:00","id":313550,"title":"","content":"Another title you might want to play around with this\u2026 Defectors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:04:22-07:00","id":622583,"title":"","content":"While I do like the idea of an Agenda that encourages its members to go out there and interact with the other supernaturals more actively, I think that this emphasis on worshipping/serving deities other than the God-Machine is a tad restrictive. Sure, faith and your place in the cosmos are big themes, and fun to explore from the perspective of someone who has looked God in the eye and knows It is not nice. My immediate hunch would be to make them more broad in belief and operation, kinda like <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/ctl/EntitlementsLordSOTUR.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Lord Sages Of The Unknown Reaches</b></a> from Changeling 1st edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T01:02:08-07:00","id":679761,"title":"","content":"I really feel awful for saying this, but my opinion was asked, and I'm not the first to express a negative opinion here...<br /> <br /> In all honesty, this Agenda completely fails to capture me . Don't get me wrong, I understand the fluff behind it - it is a logical idea that there are Demons who want the &quot;happiness in slavery&quot;, but would rather get a new boss to work for - but still... fluff doesn't always necessitate crunch, and in this case, we have an example of why.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that all of the core 4 (? I heard something about Turncoat and Analyst Agendas somewhere, but I've never seen them, and I've gone over my copy of Flowers of Hell looking) Agendas are clearly distinguished from each other, but the Traitors Agenda fails to stand out as anything more than &quot;Integrators, but seeking a True God over the God-Machine&quot;.<br /> <br /> The philosophy is sound, but the execution of it as an Agenda in its own right is just too lackluster.<br /> <br /> I could easily spin any of the corebook Agendas as a &quot;Godseeker&quot;, and what is right here in the opening post is pretty much a textbook Godseeker-Integrator, in my book.<br /> <br /> I don't see the point in it as its own Agenda at the moment, and frankly that's probably why an official equivalent hasn't yet appeared: too much of a characterization motif without anything substantial to build distinctive mechanics around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T03:46:13-07:00","id":679819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11983-new-agenda-traitors?p=679761#post679761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem here is that all of the core 4 (? I heard something about Turncoat and Analyst Agendas somewhere, but I've never seen them, and I've gone over my copy of Flowers of Hell looking)</div> </div> </div> </div>Turncoat is a nickname for the Integrator Agenda in the core book. Analyst is a new Incarnation, not an Agenda, and its in the Interface book.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the end, Agendas are primarily two things. One, a Condition. Two, an approach to Hell. The core four do hit on rejection, build it, New Dawn/Golconda/Ascension it, and fight for it. There's not a lot of approaches that won't touch on the latter four. The Condition, however, can be different. Its like how, in VtR, the Jullii are a different clan from Ventrue but are still very similar, and new covenants often end up as variations on the core five (plus Brood/VII). There's only so much room you can cover before everything starts to overlap. However, that doesn't mean we can't come up with new ways to approach the same general thing. So what if it overlaps? Should we just say that all Changeling Courts must follow the Seasonal? There's no room for new vampire covenants because of the thematic overlap with the Carthians or some other one?<br /> <br /> Even if we argue that we're just creating variations on the Conditions for each of the agendas, isn't that worth looking at too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-27-2015, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T12:12:27-07:00","id":680242,"title":"","content":"To be fair, this could be folded in with the Tempters and certain Integrators-hell, the Integrators have a factional philosophy that is basically this.. But I think there's enough interest and direction in the idea to at least give it some powerful validity as homebrew. Given the line it straddles, it can work real well in certain games as a way to break expectations, and it's broad enough to not be dependent on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-27-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}